  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1258 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nOur main upper level low eventually exits to the northeast by \nTuesday however guidance continues to keep lingering shortwave \nenergy behind the system into Tuesday night. With the continued \npresence of some coastal troughing to the south we will keep in some \nlow end pops (20-30%) across the area, favoring along and east of \nthe I-35 corridor. Wednesday into Thursday a longwave trough then \nbecomes established stretching from the Ohio Valley into the \nMississippi valley. Eventually this energy will advance \nsoutheastward from the Central plains into East Texas/Texarkana \nregion on the western periphery of aforementioned troughing. This \nshould help advance a weak cold front across our region at some \npoint either Wednesday or Wednesday night. The northwest flow that \noccurs behind this front will bring in some drier air and finally \npush any lingering rain chances over our eastern areas more to the \nsoutheast and out of our area by Wednesday night.\n\nRegarding high temps, Tuesday we should see highs rebound slightly \nback into the low 70s for those that see breaks in the clouds and \nsome more sunshine. However, by Wednesday we begin to return to more \nnormal values for this time of year with everyone getting into the \nlow to mid 70s. By Thursday a potential front begins to move \nthrough, thus we should see highs drop back a couple of degrees into \nthe low 70s with this trend continuing through Friday and into the \nweekend. Lows will trend slightly cooler with many seeing mid 50s \nmidweek before several areas taste there first 40s of the season to \nbegin the the first half of the weekend. Lows Sunday should be \nslightly warmer with most seeing the return of low to mid 50s.",
